/-!
# Order of j at a cusp place equals minus its width

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.ord_eq_neg_width_of_order_eq_mul_ord_of_qExpansion_slash`
(`27029e69-a7fd-5070-ad3e-a711c65e1ab9`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `3170cc39-04c6-5e43-aa52-37e919e8b68d`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $\Gamma\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ be a subgroup of finite index containing the translation
matrix $T$ and satisfying the predicate `CongruenceSubgroup.IsCongruenceSubgroup`, and let
$F_0\subseteq \mathbb Q((q))$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q((q))/\mathbb Q$ equal to
[`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), the subfield of $\mathbb
Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g)$
of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms $f,g$ of a common weight $k$ on $\Gamma$ (with the
denominator nonzero). Write $F$ for [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ
F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the intermediate field of $\mathbb C((q))/\mathbb C$
generated by the coefficientwise image of $F_0$. Let $y\in F$ have Laurent series $\mathrm{jqModC}$,
i.e. $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\mathbb C((q))$ of the integral power series $E_4^3\,\eta^{-24}$,
and let $\sigma\in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, $N=[\,\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z):\text{normal core of
}\Gamma\,]$. Assume given a ring homomorphism $\Phi\colon F\to\mathbb C((q))$, a place $P$ of $F$
over $\mathbb C$ (a valuation subring containing $\mathbb C$, proper, and a principal ideal ring)
and an integer $e>0$ such that: whenever $x\in F$, $k\in\mathbb Z$ and $g,h$ are modular forms of
weight $k$ on $\Gamma$ with $h\ne 0$ and $x\cdot \widetilde q_1(h)=\widetilde q_1(g)$ in $\mathbb
C((q))$, then $\Phi(x)\cdot \widetilde q_N(h\mid_k\sigma)=\widetilde q_N(g\mid_k\sigma)$, where
$\widetilde q_w$ denotes the $q$-expansion of period $w$ viewed in $\mathbb C((q))$;
$\mathrm{ord}(\Phi x)=e\cdot \mathrm{ord}_P(x)$ for all $x\ne 0$; and $\mathrm{ord}(\Phi y)=-N$.
Assume further the degree condition $[\,F:\mathbb C(y)\,]=[\,\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb
Z):\Gamma\vee\langle -1\rangle\,]$, and let $h>0$ be a natural number with $\sigma
T^{h}\sigma^{-1}\in \Gamma\vee\langle -1\rangle$ which is minimal with this property among positive
integers. Then $\mathrm{ord}_P(y)=-h$.

This identifies the order of vanishing of the modular invariant $j$ at the cusp place of the
function field of $X(\Gamma)$ read off at $\sigma\infty$ as minus the width of that cusp for
$\pm\Gamma$, the degree hypothesis guaranteeing that the field $F$ is the full function field. It
feeds the analysis of the behaviour of elements of $F$ near the cusps, being used in
[`ModularCurve.exists_tendsto_realizeOf_mul_exp_of_not_mem_toValuationSubring`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_tendsto_realizeOf_mul_exp_of_not_mem_toValuationSubring).

